Link the Roamer          St:18/59 Dx:17 Co:18 In:8 Wi:16 Ch:8  Lawful
Astral Plane $:1  HP:296(296) Pw:62(62) AC:-46 Exp:21 T:65030

#  long sword         [Basic]
#  club               [Expert]
#  sling              [Expert]
a - knock                  1*   matter       100%
w - the blessed rustproof +7 Excalibur (weapon in hand)

Cavemen weren't as bad as I thought they would be.  Even though slings
don't do very much damage, I practically get infinite ammo for the
slings, which means that if anything really bad happens, then I can
get a large stack of rocks, and just sling those from far away.    The
scrolls of earth from sokoban are really exciting for cavemen, because
it's basically instant ammo, in case things get so bad that I can't
leave the area to find a spare boulder.

I ended up spending most the game wearing leather equipment instead of
metal equipment, so that I could carry more rocks with me.

Most of the time I just hit stuff with the club the caveman got when
he started the game.  When I finally found a non-Mines altar, I
converted it, then #offered corpses until I got my first weapon gift.
This is great for lawfuls, as you either will get Grawyswandir, or you
will unlock the long sword skill.  I ended up unlocking the long sword
skill, so I #dipped for Excalibur, then used that for the rest of the
game.

I learned 1 spell the entire game, and the only purpose of that spell
was to get me confused for purposes of scroll reading.



