The Priest class is like an awful version of the Healer class.  Yes,
the auto B/U/C priest ability allowed me to get a really good AC
because I didn't mind trying on every piece of equipment in the
dungeon, it basically meant I was stuck with metal armor, which meant
that I didn't bother with casting spells for the first half of the
game.  On the other hand, my Healers automatically get 9 points of
protection AC in the beginning of the game, which means that when they
wear leather equipment, their AC ends up being better than the
Priest's AC.  And Healers had way more survivability than Priests,
since the Healers have a stethoscope and healing spells, and they
functionally get infinite food due to the stone to flesh spell.

The Priest ditched the starting mace for clubs, because my characters
like to hit a bunch of rust traps, and it's much easier to replace
clubs than maces.  When I got a unicorn horn, then I used that as my
main weapon.  After I got the castle wand, and was thus able to highly
enchant a weapon, I switched to a silver saber for the rest of the
game.  For most of the game I used darts as my main ranged weapon --
and the sling was used against monsters that are in the water, so that
I wouldn't lose darts in the water.  After I got the castle wand, I
polypiled spellbooks until I got books of magic missile and magic
mapping.  At that point, magic missile became my main ranged weapon.

And the RNG decided to give me a spellbook of identify in the mid-
game, so that my auto B/U/C priest ability could be even less exciting
than it was before.



