After playing a Ranger, I realized how much I hate Rogues.  An Elf
Ranger does a lot of damage with their starting arrows.  And mixing
random potions together can easily result in a potion of sickness,
which boosts the arrow damage even more.

The best part of the Ranger's arrow attack is that they start with so
many arrows, that even if I'm stuck in a really bad situation, I can
fire like 30 arrows and still have a bunch leftover in case something
else bad happens.  And they start with so many arrows that I never ran
out of arrows even though they disappeared at a high rate.  Compare
this to a Rogue, which only did decent damage when it could backstab.
Yes, backstab damage is great, but it basically revolved around
Elbereth + projectile weapons.  This required you to get close to the
monsters, so that you can scare them, so that they can run around in
random directions, so that you can chase them around and throw
projectiles all over the place.  It was a complete pain to pick up all
the projectiles after this was done.  However, the Ranger got to line
up the monsters, fire a bunch of arrows, and pick up all the arrows by
walking in a straight line.

As long as you know when to melee with daggers, and when you should
hit stuff with arrows -- then you don't have to worry about running
out of arrows, even though they disappear at a high rate (when you
don't have a maxed luckstone).

This was the first game where I went into Gehennom with a cruddy
ascension kit.  The game didn't randomly generate any really good
equipment, and polypiling all the magic items in the game didn't give
really good equipment either.  I ended up needing the haste self and
levitation spells, as I couldn't find equipment for those things
before Gehennom.  I did get a spellbook of detect treasure through
polypiling, which I used in Gehennom to find the rest of my ascension
kit.  Even after all that, I ended up ascending with AC -19, which is
the worst ascending AC I've ever had.  However, it turns out that an
AC of -19 was completely fine, since I had 259 HP.

This leads to the very important discovery that using marker charges
for 2 cursed genocide scrolls, is much better than using those charges
for 4 blessed enchant armor scrolls, as the HP boost from reversed
genocided nurses is way more important than the AC boost you would
have gotten from the extra enchant armor scrolls.  I got 259 HP even
though I didn't alchemy any potions of full healing in this game (I
couldn't alchemy a stack of full healing potions this game because I
used all the non-full-healing potions for either potions of sickness
or potions of holy water).

This is also the second ascension in a row where the game didn't give
me any bags of holding, so I'm getting used to only carrying around
what I really need.


